# Accessibility

For every interactive component:

- Start from correct native semantics where possible.
- Follow the applicable WAI-ARIA interaction pattern for custom widgets.
- Test keyboard navigation, Escape behavior and focus restoration when relevant.
- Never hide a focusable element from accessibility APIs while it remains focusable.
- Disabled controls must not trigger user actions.
- Labels, descriptions and errors must be programmatically associated with their controls.
- Focus-visible styling must remain usable in all supported themes.
- Modals/drawers/popovers must have deliberate focus and dismissal behavior.
